lse,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"ST017\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"The answer covers all required elements. It requires pre-open daily holdings with identifiers, descriptions, quantities and weights, matching the NAV-basis holdings. It gives prior-business-day NAV, market price and premium/discount, plus premium/discount history and a 30-day median spread. It states the >2% for more than seven consecutive trading days statement with contributing factors, posted by the next trading day and kept at least one year.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":0,\"reason\":\"The answer says only 'table or chart of daily premiums/discounts.' It does not mention a table counting days at premium or discount. It gives no spread method: no NBBO observations at 10-second intervals and no normalization by midpoint. 'Most recent 30 days' alone does not meet the minimum.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"The answer gives the most recent calendar year plus completed quarters since, with full life for younger funds. The header states the disclosures are public and free.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"No central error: the answer makes holdings disclosure mandatory and correctly says baskets need no daily website publication, only policies and records. 'Table or chart' slightly understates the rule, which requires both a table and a line graph, but this is an imprecision rather than a material falsehood. Coverage sums to 2 of 3, which is at least half, but point 2 is missing, so the grade is partial rather than correct.\"}","ttft_ms":7441,"type":"result","duration_ms":11854,"uuid":"92510f73-c58a-4bd7-b678-512c2301476f","ttft_stream_ms":1160,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":1161,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
